    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and every value derived from it follows suit.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.generateCustomerCode`** \u2014 replaced the old `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` sequence-based code with `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n   - `REGION` is derived via `LocalityLookup.forPostcodeAndCity(postcode, city)` (postcode-first, per the region lookup).\n   - `HASH8` is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`.\n   - The per-city sequence number is dropped entirely.\n   - The call site now passes the already-normalized telephone, postcode, city and last name.\n\n2. **Extracted `sha256UpperHex(input, length)`** helper for the customer-code hash. (I left `generateHouseholdId` untouched \u2014 its separator is a pre-existing NUL byte in the source, not the space its Javadoc claims; refactoring it would have silently changed household-id behavior, which is out of scope.)\n\n3. **Membership number & check digit** \u2014 these already build from `customerCode` (`generateMembershipNumber` appends `-M<YY>`, `Owner.getCheckDigit()` runs Luhn over the code's digits), so they automatically move to the new identity. Only the doc example was updated.\n\n4. **Audit record** \u2014 already logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it now emits the new code (verified in the run: `AUDIT - Owner created: ... customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ...`).\n\n5. **Locality derivation** \u2014 added `LocalityLookup.forCustomerCode(...)` which returns the `REGION` component of the customer code (falling back to the old postcode/city lookup for owners without a code, e.g. seed data), and pointed the `OwnerMapper` locality mapping at it. Locality now comes from the region-and-hash identity.\n\n**Result:** `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The acceptance test confirms `customerCode` matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`.",
